  "implemented": [
    "Opaque public Seed exports ordered commitments and sorted nullifiers without private notes, amounts, owners, keys or witnesses",
    "Bounded exact-length wire decoding checks both counts before allocating leaf lists",
    "Bootstrap authenticates chain/pool/code/factory scope, retained epoch and native state root, then reconstructs both canonical roots and note count",
    "Foreign local sequence numbers and Irmin commits are not portable authority; each importing node resolves its own canonical head",
    "Version 2 encrypted journals store public seed segments and preserve version 1 recovery",
    "Explicit reanchor repairs only public index state, preserving accepted limits and cumulative consumed update budget",
    "Isolated application graphs accept an Irmin proof of the original genesis opt-in, tied to the configured full genesis root and exact chain/profile metadata",
    "Checkpoint readers can return the independently configured genesis root without inventing an epoch record, transaction or retained genesis snapshot",
    "Current public or mutable metadata cannot enable an isolated application profile or replace its original genesis proof"
  ],
